---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Port PRs or missing commits to another series; maintainer sweeps; blacklists

Usage: odx port [OPTIONS]
       odx port <COMMAND>

Commands:
  pr         Port one pull request to another series: its commits cherry-picked with their authors onto the branch `<to>-port-<n>`, then odoo-lint's upgrade fixes
  addon      Port the commits an addon has on another series and lacks on the target, grouped by pull request, on the branch `<to>-port-<addon>`
  blacklist  Add an entry to an addon's oca-port blacklist and commit it on the branch checked out: `.oca/oca-port/blacklist/<addon>.json`, written as oca-port writes it
  sweep      Check every addon of the target series against older series (maintainer mode): portable pull requests and false positives (migration commits, repo-wide changes, translations)
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml or repos.yaml to use

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --offline
          Serve forge and index data from the cache only. Only network calls are skipped: local work (git, pre-commit, odoo-lint) takes as long as before

      --continue
          Go on after resolving a conflict

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --abort
          Give up the port in progress and delete its branch

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale. Like --offline, this saves network time only

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase log verbosity (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version
